flowchart TB
    accTitle: The whole app — ask, process, and explore
    accDescr: Follow the numbered connectors. The server checks the question and recent context. When fresh database data is needed, first read the cached schema, fetching it from PostgreSQL if missing; next ask the AI provider to generate SQL using that schema; then validate and execute the SQL against PostgreSQL. Only after rows return does the server optionally ask the AI provider to explain them. Without an explanation, return the SQL and table directly. Questions that need no fresh data can receive a direct answer or clarification. Progress updates, schema browsing, cancellation, and local result exploration support this journey.
    %% Companion guide: docs/architecture.md

    BROWSER["Your workspace: Ask, follow up, and watch progress"]:::view
    SERVER["App server: Check the question and recent context"]:::work
    CACHED_SCHEMA["Read the cached database schema: Fetch from PostgreSQL if missing"]:::data
    WRITE_SQL["AI provider: Write SQL using the question and schema"]:::work
    QUERY["Validate and execute read-only SQL: PostgreSQL returns matching rows"]:::data
    EXPLAIN["AI provider: Explain the returned rows only after execution"]:::work
    DIRECT["Answer from available context or ask for clarification"]:::work
    RESPONSE["Back in your workspace: Answer, table, warnings, or error"]:::view
    EXPLORE["Explore the loaded rows: Sort, page, resize, or export CSV"]:::view
    SCHEMA["Browse tables and columns: Load or refresh the saved list"]:::data
    CANCEL["Cancel the current turn or start a new chat when idle"]:::note

    BROWSER -->|1. Submit question| SERVER
    SERVER -->|2.a. Fresh data needed| CACHED_SCHEMA
    CACHED_SCHEMA -->|3. Schema ready| WRITE_SQL
    WRITE_SQL -->|4. SQL generated| QUERY
    QUERY -->|5.a. Explanation enabled| EXPLAIN
    EXPLAIN -->|6. Explanation or warning| RESPONSE
    QUERY -->|5.b. Explanation disabled| RESPONSE
    SERVER -->|2.b. No fresh data needed| DIRECT
    DIRECT -->|3.b. Direct response| RESPONSE
    RESPONSE -->|7. Explore results| EXPLORE
    BROWSER -.->|Optional| SCHEMA
    BROWSER -.->|Optional| CANCEL

    classDef view fill:#eff6ff,stroke:#2563eb,color:#172033,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef work fill:#f5f3ff,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#4c1d95,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef data fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef note fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#d97706,color:#78350f,stroke-width:1.5px;
